# What every reader of fixtures/kv4badv.store must answer (W-ES-P8D 2026-10-30): A REFUSAL BY NAME.
# kv4deep with bit 0 of the first value cell of the first non-empty value flipped (VAL object 1240 under
# leaf 2813 at MIN_FANOUT since W-ES-HARD -- object 1210 at fanout 8; crc not re-sealed). Measured
# native: Tree(BadCrc { obj: 1240, want: 1977864513, got: Some(3108622815) }).
# BAD_CRC = 10 on every reader; bebop.bin prints -10.
status=10
# RE-ANCHORED (conform kv4.rs `reanchor`, 2026-10-30): the corrupted cell lies inside the live commit's
# range, so the superblock's anchor (FORMAT §7, cell 9) and its crc are recomputed over the corrupted
# bytes. Before that, bebop.bin's st_open fell back to generation k-1 (`kv.bin g` 5, n=125) and the C
